<Window x:Class="VaccineAssist.Desktop.Views.AgePromptWindow"
        xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
        xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
        Title="Patient age"
        Width="340" SizeToContent="Height"
        WindowStyle="ToolWindow"
        Topmost="True"
        ShowInTaskbar="False"
        ResizeMode="NoResize"
        WindowStartupLocation="CenterScreen"
        Loaded="AgePromptWindow_OnLoaded"
        PreviewKeyDown="AgePromptWindow_OnPreviewKeyDown">
    <!--
        Originally Ctrl+Keypad 4 (Will, 2026-09-25, verbatim): "Add new
        hotkey Ctrl+Keypad 4 that shows a screen to enter patient age,
        then shows the macro codes page filtered to only show vaccines
        suitable for their age range..." This is that screen. Re-keyed
        same day, round 2 (Will, verbatim): "Fro the new ctrl+keypad 4
        item, make it ctrl+keypad 2 to start it..." — the hotkey that
        opens this window is now Ctrl+Keypad 2 (see MainWindow's
        _ageMacroHotKey/GlobalHotKey.VK_NUMPAD2); this window itself is
        unaffected by which hotkey opens it.

        No Owner (unlike TextEntryPromptWindow/VarUpdateConfirmationWindow's
        Owner=owner convention) — same "no guaranteed visible owner"
        reasoning as MacroCodesWindow: this is reached straight from a
        global hotkey, and MainWindow is very often hidden to the tray at
        that point (see MainWindow's own class doc comment), so
        WindowStartupLocation="CenterScreen"/Topmost/ShowInTaskbar="False"
        match MacroCodesWindow.xaml's shell instead.

        Years is required (0-120, same range DataEntryPopupViewModel's own
        age stage validates). See AgePromptInput (pure parse/validate,
        shared with the OK button's enabled state below) and
        MainWindow.ShowAgeMacroPrompt for how the result feeds
        AgeMacroCodesUrlBuilder + MacroCodesWindow.

        2026-09-25 round 2 (Will, verbatim): "We don't vaccicne less than
        age 3, so remove the months indicator." Months input dropped —
        years-only, single box.
    -->
    <StackPanel Margin="16">
        <TextBlock Text="Patient age" FontWeight="Bold"/>
        <StackPanel Margin="0,12,0,0">
            <TextBlock Text="Years"/>
            <TextBox x:Name="YearsTextBox" Width="70"
                     PreviewTextInput="AgeTextBox_OnPreviewTextInput"
                     TextChanged="AgeTextBox_OnTextChanged"
                     KeyDown="AgeTextBox_OnKeyDown"/>
        </StackPanel>
        <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" HorizontalAlignment="Right" Margin="0,16,0,0">
            <Button x:Name="OkButton" Content="OK" Padding="12,4" Margin="0,0,8,0"
                    IsEnabled="False" IsDefault="True" Click="OkButton_OnClick"/>
            <Button Content="Cancel" Padding="12,4" IsCancel="True" Click="CancelButton_OnClick"/>
        </StackPanel>
    </StackPanel>
</Window>
